   "gap": "Durrett PTE author version 5 of 11 January 2019, Appendix A.1, p. 458 (PDF p. 466), introduces mu*(E) = inf of sums of mu(A_i) over covers with the justification that any measure nu agreeing with mu on the algebra satisfies nu(E) <= nu(union A_i) <= sum nu(A_i) = sum mu(A_i), so mu* is an upper bound for every extension on its domain (the measurable sets being those where this bound is tight). The handbook definition (measure-extension.tex lines 127-139) gives no justification of the cover formula, and this domination of every extension by mu* is neither stated nor proved anywhere on the route.",
