   "gap": "Durrett PTE author version 5 of 11 January 2019, p. 3 (PDF p. 11), with Theorem 1.1.4, justifies the interval convention: the choice of intervals closed on the right is dictated by the identity that the intersection of (a, b_n] over n is (a, b] when b_n decreases to b, and the choice open on the left is explained by the semialgebra complement property. The handbook definition (measure-extension.tex lines 168-195) fixes the convention without this justification, and it is not supplied anywhere on the route; the endpoint warning (lines 340-356) shows only that a function that is not right continuous cannot be a cumulative distribution.",
